{"query":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1000,"description":"A TraceQL query, for example { resource.service.name = \"payments-api\" && status = error }"},"minutes":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":120,"default":15},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":20,"default":10}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"get_trace","title":"Get a trace","description":"The spans of one trace, in start order: service, operation, timing, status, key attributes and exception events. A webhook's trace runs from the receiver through Kafka to both consumers. A long trace keeps its first and its last spans.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"trace_id":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-fA-F]{1,32}$","description":"A trace id, as found by search_traces or in a log line's trace_id"}},"required":["trace_id"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"service_health","title":"Service health","description":"Each container of the payments system: running or not, its health check, restarts, and when it started.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"recent_deploys","title":"Recent deploys","description":"When each service's container was last created (a deploy, a restart with new settings, or a rollback), newest first, with its image and its behavior settings: LEDGER_HANDLER, CONFIRMER_HANDLER, BAD_EVENTS, PROVIDER_BREAKER, CHARGE_AMOUNT_UNIT, REFUND_CONNECTION, WEBHOOK_SECRET_VERSION. No other setting is shown.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"money_check","title":"Money check","description":"Reconcile our books with the payment provider's own records: five invariants (every provider event posted exactly once; the ledger balanced; the ledger matching the provider; our payments matching the provider's; our refunds matching the provider's). With wait=true it first waits until everything up to now is handled; if that cannot happen, the outcome is 'could not run', and the reason is itself a symptom. With wait=false events still in flight look lost.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"wait":{"type":"boolean","default":true,"description":"true: first wait until everything up to now is handled. false: check right away"},"timeout_seconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":5,"maximum":120,"default":60}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}}],"server":{"name":"klaxon-ops","version":"0.0.1","protocol":"2025-11-25"}}
